meta {
  name: Send WhatsApp To Lead
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/leads/{{leadId}}/whatsapp
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "template_id": "{{whatsappTemplateId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Sends an approved WhatsApp template to the lead.

  The body names ONLY the template: the destination number is read from the
  lead server-side, and the message text comes from the Meta-approved template,
  so a caller can neither redirect the send nor supply its own copy. Take
  template_id from List-WhatsApp-Templates.

  Requires the lms.leads.whatsapp.send capability (sales_representative and
  above) plus edit access to this particular lead. A read_only user gets 403.

  On success a `whatsapp` row is written to lms.lead_interactions and shows up
  in the lead's activity timeline. A failed Interakt send returns 502 and
  writes nothing.
}
